{"name":"Knit Cardigan","hex":"#6d6c5f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"knit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn thread or yarn into a piece of fabric by forming loops that are pulled through each other. This can be done by hand with needles or by machine.","To create a stitch by pulling the working yarn through an existing stitch from back to front."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A knitted garment.","A session of knitting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knit"},{"term":"cardigan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of sweater or jumper that fastens up the front with buttons or a zipper, usually machine- or hand-knitted from wool."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardigan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cardigan (sweater)","blocks":[{"text":"A cardigan is a type of knitted garment that has an open front and is worn like a jacket."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/NMA.0038588%2C_Fashion_Photo_by_Erik_Holm%C3%A9n_1947.jpg/330px-NMA.0038588%2C_Fashion_Photo_by_Erik_Holm%C3%A9n_1947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardigan_(sweater)","wikidata":"Q877140"},{"title":"Cardigan (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cardigan\" is a song by the American singer-songwriter Taylor Swift and the lead single from her eighth studio album, Folklore (2020). Republic Records released the song on July 24, 2020. Written by Swift and its producer, Aaron Dessner, \"Cardigan\" is a soft rock, folk, and indie rock ballad, with a stripped-down arrangement of a piano, drums, and violins."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Taylor_Swift_-_Cardigan.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardigan_(song)","wikidata":"Q97631372"},{"title":"Knitting","blocks":[{"text":"Knitting is the process of interloo